      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L13-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "13.2: Polynomial Long Division",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\((x-2)\\) is a factor of \\(2x^3 - 7x^2 + x + 10\\), which means there is some other factor \\(A\\) where \\(2x^3 - 7x^2 + x + 10=(x-2)(A)\\). Finish the division started here to find the value of \\(A\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L13-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "13.2: Polynomial Long Division",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle \\displaystyle \\require{enclose} \\begin{array}{r} 2x+1 \\enclose{longdiv}{2x^3+13x^2+16x+5} \\end{array}\\)",
