    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L13-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "13.4: Missing Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "In earlier grades, we learned how to add, subtract, and multiply numbers. We also learned that one way to divide numbers, like 1573 divided by 11, is by using long division.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L13-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "13.4: Missing Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Here the division has been completed in stages, focusing on the highest power of 10 (1,000) in the dividend 1,573, and working down. This long division shows that \\(1573 = (11)(143)\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L13-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "13.4: Missing Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Similar to integers, we can add, subtract, and multiply polynomials. It turns out that we can also use long division on polynomials. Instead of focusing on powers of 10, in polynomial long division we focus on powers of \\(x\\). Just as we…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L13-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "13.4: Missing Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle \\displaystyle \\displaystyle \\require{enclose} \\begin{array}{r} x^2\\phantom{+7x+33} \\\\ x+1 \\enclose{longdiv}{x^3+5x^2+7x+3} \\\\ \\underline{\\text-x^3-x^2} \\phantom{+7x+333} \\\\ 4x^2+7x \\phantom{+33}\\\\ \\end{array}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
